preConditionHook:
// Brooks's credibility test for a leg: the leg that breaks the trend line and
// the leg that tests the extreme both have to be long enough to mean something.
// Both of the last two legs must run at least minLegBars bars -- the gap
// between the last two CONFIRMED swing lows, and the bars since the most recent
// one.
//
// The pivot scan is INLINED rather than reaching into SwingHigh.json -- rules
// in this corpus never reference each other -- and mirrors the EL twin's
// SwingLowBar at Occurrence 1 and 2.
//
// MEASURED, EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt (@ES 60 min):
//   * the pivot test is MIXED -- the pivot low is AT OR BELOW the swingStrength
//     OLDER bars and STRICTLY BELOW the swingStrength NEWER bars (the mirror of
//     the measured high-side rule; the probe's flat-extreme series was a flat
//     TOP only). Bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER index the NEWER bar, so
//     the strict half is the k < j loop;
//   * the confirmation lag is exactly swingStrength bars, never 0 or 1, which
//     both makes the scan lookahead-safe and bounds loB2 below by
//     swingStrength;
//   * pivotLookback is EL's Length: candidate offsets 0..pivotLookback-1 from
//     the current bar inclusive, and the neighbourhood test reaches
//     swingStrength bars PAST the window, so the deepest index touched is
//     pivotLookback - 1 + swingStrength;
//   * a window with no pivot returns the -1 SENTINEL. Scanning newest-first and
//     taking the first two hits reproduces Occurrence 1 and 2; fewer than two
//     is the sentinel case, guarded below because -1 compares SMALLER than any
//     real bar count and would otherwise fail the test silently for the wrong
//     reason. Occurrence 3+ is UNMEASURED and is not asked for;
//   * the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance, hence el_lt /
//     el_le inside the scan rather than raw < and <=.
// No WFSafe_SwingLow exists, so plain EL governs.
//
// SIDES ARE IDENTICAL, per the merge's 'same'. The rule is a size test in BARS,
// not a price comparison, so there is nothing to flip; the swing-low series is
// the one the merged pseudocode and description both name, and the swing-high
// spelling is the recorded alternative rather than the short side. Placing this
// beside a directional rule is what gives it a direction.
//
// It measures legs by SWING PIVOTS, not by the decided H1/H2 counter of
// HighLowBarCount (R17-01), so the leg_counting family may hold a behaviourally
// different rule with the same intent. Brooks's exception -- one leg may be one
// or two exceptionally large bars instead -- is not mechanized.
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the
// generator only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration
// is a redefinition when this rule is placed twice in one strategy.
// Every one is fully assigned each bar before it is read.
pivS = (int)swingStrength;
pivW = (int)pivotLookback;
loB1 = -1.0;
loB2 = -1.0;
foundLo = 0;
for (int j = pivS; j <= pivW - 1; ++j) {
    bool ok = true;
    for (int k = j - pivS; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) { ok = false; break; }
    }
    if (ok) {
        for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + pivS; ++k) {
            if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) { ok = false; break; }
        }
    }
    if (ok) {
        ++foundLo;
        if (foundLo == 1) { loB2 = (double)j; }
        else { loB1 = (double)j; break; }
    }
}
haveLegs = (foundLo == 2) && (loB1 != -1.0) && (loB2 != -1.0);
legsLongEnough = haveLegs && el_ge(loB1 - loB2, minLegBars) && el_ge(loB2, minLegBars);
